# Local Terraform runs (Scaleway)

PowerShell:

    $env:SCW_ACCESS_KEY="<scaleway access key>"
    $env:SCW_SECRET_KEY="<scaleway secret key>"
    $env:SCW_DEFAULT_PROJECT_ID="<project id>"
    $env:SCW_DEFAULT_ORGANIZATION_ID="<organization id>"
    $env:TF_VAR_scw_project_id=$env:SCW_DEFAULT_PROJECT_ID
    # Remote state uses the S3-compatible API on Scaleway Object Storage
    $env:AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=$env:SCW_ACCESS_KEY
    $env:AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=$env:SCW_SECRET_KEY
    $env:TF_VAR_database_url="<postgres connection string>"

    terraform init/plan/apply/destroy

Notes:
- The state bucket `slay-drip-tfstate` (region fr-par) must exist before `terraform init`.
- Build and push the API image (backend/lambda) before the first `apply`, because the
  container is deployed from `rg.fr-par.scw.cloud/slay-drip-<env>/api:latest`.
- `AWS_*` variables are only used because Terraform's S3 backend reads them. Nothing here talks to AWS.
